From 5a1da0ae1bac995707f1a4dee41c7935f538a51c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dan <Dan Kennedy>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:27:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] When a b-tree cell is deleted, zero the cursor's cell-info
 cache as the cell it describes no longer exists, even if the cursor position
 is being preserved. Report [bugs:/info/2026-10-18T16:11:58Z |
 2026-10-18T16:11:58Z].

[Hades: backport to 3.54.1 from branch-3.54. The release is the amalgamation, so the change is made where src/btree.c in sqlite3.c. Not carried: test/delete4.test (tests of the source tree).]

FossilOrigin-Name: 07ed30558ee7da460ed0ca2b36cd555aeb5caa91f0971b2cf83adc08524ca9b7
Upstream: https://sqlite.org/src/info/07ed30558ee7da460ed0ca2b36cd555aeb5caa91f0971b2cf83adc08524ca9b7
---
 sqlite3.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sqlite3.c b/sqlite3.c
index 20553b4..8e31ea7 100644
--- a/sqlite3.c
+++ b/sqlite3.c
@@ -82813,6 +82813,12 @@ SQLITE_PRIVATE int sqlite3BtreeDelete(BtCursor *pCur, u8 flags){
       }else{
         pCur->skipNext = 1;
       }
+      /* The pCur->info structure is currently populated with the details
+      ** of the cell that was just removed. But pCur->ix now points to a
+      ** different cell in the b-tree. So zero info.nSize here so that if
+      ** saveCursorPosition() is called on this cursor it does not trust
+      ** the contents of pCur->info.  */
+      pCur->info.nSize = 0;
     }else{
       rc = moveToRoot(pCur);
       if( bPreserve ){
